        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Deck stain drying time</strong> runs one to two hours to the touch and four to six to walk on for water-based, four to twelve and 24 hours for oil-based, with full cure at one to three days for both. The number that governs your weekend is rain safety, and 24 hours is the honest answer regardless of what the fast-dry claims promise.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The two failures worth designing around are <strong class="text-white">wet wood and heavy application</strong>. Wait 48 to 72 hours after washing, check moisture with a meter or a sprinkle test, apply thin, and wipe back anything the boards have not taken in fifteen minutes.
          </p>
